chapter AFP

session Datalog_Graph = Datalog_Certification +
  description \<open>Datalog-to-graph (Path 2 of the certificate foundedness story). First the purely
    graph-theoretic fact that a finite directed graph has a topological numbering iff it has no
    (directed) cycle (\<open>Graph_Topological_Order\<close>), then the bridge: convert a datalog certificate to
    the graph library's \<open>dgraph\<close> support graph and discharge the foundedness obligation
    \<open>dl_founded\<close> from acyclicity of that graph (\<open>Datalog_To_Graph\<close>). The graph library
    (Directed_Set_Graphs) is pulled in HERE -- and only here -- so its imperative/Separation_Logic
    stack never meets the AFP Collections/ODE tower of the PDDL branch.

    \<open>DFS_DirCycle_Linear{_Aux}\<close> are PDDL-free graph-library extensions rather than datalog
    theories: the directed counterpart of the library's \<open>DFS_Cycles\<close>, i.e. a whole-graph
    (linear) cycle search whose outer loop seeds each inner directed-cycle DFS with the region
    the earlier calls already finished. They live here because this is the session that owns
    the graph-library dependency; they belong upstream once stable.\<close>
  options [timeout = 600]
  sessions
    "Directed_Set_Graphs"
    "Directed_Cycle_DFS"
  theories
    Graph_Topological_Order
    Datalog_To_Graph
    Datalog_Cycle_DFS
    Datalog_Cycle_DFS_Global
    Datalog_Certificate_Index
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear_Aux
    DFS_DirCycle_Linear
